
# Firebase Studio

This is a NextJS starter in Firebase Studio.

To get started, take a look at src/app/page.tsx.

## Developer notes

- CI: A GitHub Actions workflow is added at `.github/workflows/ci.yml` which runs `npm ci`, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build` on pushes and PRs to `main`/`master`.
- Linting/Formatting: `.eslintrc.json` and `.prettierrc` were added. Install dev deps locally and run `npm run lint`.
- Sentry: A small helper is available at `src/lib/sentry.ts`. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` in your environment to enable.
- Fixed: renamed/fixed UI checkbox component (`src/components/ui/checkbox.tsx`) and left a compatibility re-export at `ckeckbox.tsx`.

## Performance / Bundle Analysis

- To analyze the client bundle, install `@next/bundle-analyzer` and `cross-env` then run:

```powershell
npm install --save-dev @next/bundle-analyzer cross-env
npm run analyze
```

- I've added lazy-loading wrappers for heavy dashboard components under `src/components/quantumsage/Lazy*` to reduce initial bundle size (e.g., `LazyChartDisplay`, `LazyTechnicalIndicatorsCard`).

## Observability / Sentry

- I added server and client Sentry config files (`sentry.server.config.js` and `sentry.client.config.js`). To enable Sentry in production, set the DSN in environment variables:

```powershell
setx SENTRY_DSN "https://<key>@sentry.io/<project>"
setx NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN "https://<key>@sentry.io/<project>"
```

- A small server init helper is available at `src/lib/sentry.server.ts`. The client initializer is `src/components/SentryInit.tsx`.

- I also added a lightweight AI metrics recorder at `src/lib/aiMetrics.ts` and a simple endpoint at `/api/ai-metrics` to inspect metrics locally.

- The `/api/ai-metrics` endpoint is now protected using an API key. Set `AI_METRICS_API_KEY` in your environment, and call the endpoint with header `x-api-key: <your-key>`.
- The endpoint also has a basic in-memory rate limiter to prevent accidental abuse. For production, secure this behind internal tooling or require authenticated access.

## AI Robustness: caching & rate limiting

- A small in-memory cache is available at `src/lib/aiCache.ts`. Flows will check the cache before calling the model and store responses with a default TTL of 5 minutes.
- A global AI rate limiter protects the service from accidental overload; default limit is controlled by env `AI_GLOBAL_RATE_LIMIT` (requests per minute). When exceeded flows will throw an error.

Notes: For production, replace the in-memory cache with Redis (or equivalent) and the in-memory rate limiter with a distributed limiter (Redis tokens, cloud rate-limiting, or API gateway policies).



